Error [E0118]: Pattern hole `{root}` would make a new `root`, but `root` already holds a value
  --> pattern_hole_reuse_value.jet:2:23
    |
  2 |     return value == "{root}jet"
    |                       ^^^^
 Why: A pattern hole introduces a new name; it does not compare with an existing value or refine it
 Fix: Wrap the pattern text in parentheses to compare with the existing value, or pick a new hole name to capture
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0118
